%description:

What a real cell's background UEs cost a real UE of another cell, against the
closed form.

A background UE has no protocol stack. What its allocations do reaches the rest
of the network only as transmissions on the radio medium: in DL its base
station's radio sends one for each allocation, with the base station's power
and antenna; in UL the UE's phantom radio sends one, with the generator's power.

Worth having separately from InterferenceDelta and InterferenceDeltaUl, as the
interferer here is a cell that carries background UEs only: the cell's real
frames, the path those tests grade, do not exist in this scenario. And
separately from BackgroundUeCqi, which grades the what-ifs of such UEs and
not their allocations.

The scenario is two real cells: a real UE, the victim, in the first, with a
trickle in both directions; one background UE, loaded in both directions, in the
second, whose antenna is sectorial (ANISOTROPIC) with a boresight well off the
victim. Fading and shadowing are off, every link is NLOS by configuration, and
downlinkInterference and uplinkInterference are off in one run and on in the
other, so that the victim's four statistics take these values:

    S_DL = P1 + G1 + Gue - cableLoss_ue - PL(d_serving)
    I_DL = P2 - A(phi, theta) + G2 + Gue - cableLoss_ue - PL(d_gnb2)
    N_DL = thermalNoise + noiseFigure_ue
    S_UL = ueTxPower + Gue + G1 - cableLoss_gnb - PL(d_serving)
    I_UL = bgTxPower + Gbg + G1 - cableLoss_gnb - PL(d_bgUe)
    N_UL = thermalNoise + noiseFigure_gnb

where A is the sectorial pattern of TR 36.873 Table 7.1-1, the study a TR 38.901
cell takes it from. The victim stands on the x axis of gnb2, the boresight 60
degrees off it, so phi = 60 degrees and A is about 10 dB, the horizontal
term and a small vertical one.

The path loss and A are the specifications'; that a background UE's allocations
reach the medium with these budgets is the model's choice, so this is a regression
test of that choice.

With the switches off, every statistic is S - N. With them on, the maximum is
S - N, from the slots in which the background UE had no allocation, and the
minimum S - (N + I), from those in which it occupied every band: the reception
statistics, on the bands the victim used, and the CQI's, on all bands. Those
endpoints only occur when the allocations reach the medium. So:

 - deleting the DL allocation's transmission makes the DL minimum the quiet
   budget, or trips the debug assertion on the medium's band occupancy against
   the scheduler's (in the commits that still have it);
 - an allocation that goes out omnidirectionally moves the DL minimum by A,
   or trips the debug assertion that it does not, in the DL walk;
 - deleting the UL registration in the scheduler makes the UL minimum the quiet
   budget, or trips the debug assertion on the Binder's map (while it exists).

The background UE's own what-ifs are graded as well. In DL they pass through
the sector: at 110 m from gnb2, on its x axis, with phi = 60 degrees and the
larger vertical term of a closer UE; in UL they do not, as a UE's antenna
is not the cell's. The victim's trickle does not fill a slot, so with the
switches on only their maximum has a closed form.

Both rtx rates are 0, so all of the load is the allocations of new data, and
the loaded minimum is reached without the scheduler's rtx path. Its registration
sites are not covered here.

%extraargs: -c BackgroundUeLoad

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config BackgroundUeLoad]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.MultiCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 3s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s
seed-set = 0

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false
# The extremes are the quantities under test here, not the average.
**.bgMeasuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.bgMeasuredSinrUl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.measuredSinrUl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.rcvdSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.rcvdSinrUl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

############### The sweep: the medium's switches of a real cell's interference ##############
**.downlinkInterference = ${dli = false, true}
**.uplinkInterference = ${uli = false, true ! dli}
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

############### Geometry: the victim and the background UE on the x axis of the cells ##############
*.gnb1.mobility.initialX = 250m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialX = 750m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.numUe = 1
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1
# Association is by best signal and then frozen.
**.dynamicCellAssociation = true
**.enableHandover = false
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 350m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 500m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].numBgUes = 1
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].mobility.initialX = 640m
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1500m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one NLOS path loss and nothing else ##############
**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = false
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false

############### The budget terms, stated rather than inherited, and apart ##############
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
*.gnb1.**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
*.gnb2.**.eNodeBTxPower = 37dBm
**.ueTxPower = 25dBm
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
*.gnb1.cellularNic.radio.antenna.gain = 17dBi
*.gnb2.cellularNic.radio.antenna.gain = 15dBi
*.gnb2.cellularNic.radio.antenna.txDirection = "ANISOTROPIC"
*.gnb2.cellularNic.radio.antenna.txAngle = 120deg
*.gnb*.cellularNic.radio.receiver.noiseFigure = 4dB
*.gnb*.cellularNic.radio.receiver.cableLoss = 1dB
*.ue[*].cellularNic.*adio.antenna.gain = 1dBi
*.ue[*].cellularNic.*adio.receiver.noiseFigure = 8dB
*.ue[*].cellularNic.*adio.receiver.cableLoss = 2.5dB
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].radio.antenna.gain = 3dBi
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].radio.noiseFigure = 9dB
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].radio.cableLoss = 3.5dB
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].generator.txPower = 21dBm

############### Traffic: a trickle for the victim, a load for the background UE ##############
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.typename = "TrafficGeneratorCbr"
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.rtxRateDl = 0
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.rtxRateUl = 0
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.startTimeDl = 0.1s
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.packetSizeDl = 1000B
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.periodDl = 0.007s
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.startTimeUl = 0.1s
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.packetSizeUl = 1000B
*.gnb2.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.periodUl = 0.007s

*.ue[0].numApps = 2
*.server.numApps = 2
*.ue[0].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[0].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.013s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.ue[0].app[1].typename = "CbrSender"
*.ue[0].app[1].destAddress = "server"
*.ue[0].app[1].destPort = 4000
*.ue[0].app[1].localPort = 4088
*.ue[0].app[1].packetSize = 40B
*.ue[0].app[1].samplingTime = 0.013s
*.ue[0].app[1].startTime = 0.1s
*.server.app[1].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.server.app[1].localPort = 4000

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=27 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
